# The render graph's clang-tidy config: native/.clang-tidy (cppcoreguidelines,
# bugprone, performance, modernize — every warning an error) plus this
# directory's headers, minus the checks below, each disabled for a stated reason.
#
#   cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-avoid-unchecked-container-access
#       operator[] on std::array / std::vector / std::span. The graph's inner
#       loops are the TS renderer's uniform packing, matrix products and pixel
#       copies, ported index for index so they stay reviewable against
#       packages/renderer; `.at()` there puts a branch and a throw path into
#       every draw of every frame (the per-frame hot path CLAUDE.md guards).
#       Indices are loop-bounded by the container's own size or fixed by the
#       std140 layout; ASan (the sanitizer presets) covers them at runtime.
#   modernize-use-designated-initializers
#       Rect / Color / Vec4 / TexRef are value tuples mirroring the TS object
#       literals ({x, y, width, height}); naming every field at each of ~160
#       sites doubles the line without catching anything the distinct types
#       do not already catch.
#   clang-analyzer-optin.core.EnumCastOutOfRange
#       Device::dynamic_material hands out Mat values PAST Mat::Count_ on
#       purpose — plugin-effect and engine-owned materials share the pipeline
#       cache with the extracted builtin table (material_of checks the range).
#   bugprone-float-loop-counter, clang-analyzer-security.FloatLoopCounter
#       OverlayPass gridLines accumulates its line positions in a double loop
#       counter because the TS does (`x += spacing`): the same float
#       accumulation is what makes the same lines land on the same pixels.
Checks: >
  -cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-avoid-unchecked-container-access,
  -modernize-use-designated-initializers,
  -clang-analyzer-optin.core.EnumCastOutOfRange,
  -bugprone-float-loop-counter,
  -clang-analyzer-security.FloatLoopCounter
InheritParentConfig: true
HeaderFilterRegex: '.*(native[/\\](include|libs)|render_graph)[/\\].*'
